WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.623
Cedar Vale renews its service and adds a

00:00:02.623 --> 00:00:04.992
new recurring service in the same purchase.

00:00:05.242 --> 00:00:07.461
There is also a one-time commissioning fee.

00:00:07.711 --> 00:00:10.208
We'll use an illustrated example to separate

00:00:10.208 --> 00:00:12.483
the purchase total, recurring value and

00:00:12.483 --> 00:00:14.683
growth, then check what a report should

00:00:14.683 --> 00:00:15.092
show.

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:18.211
Keep the prior agreement, current purchase

00:00:18.211 --> 00:00:19.628
and report date beside you.

00:00:19.878 --> 00:00:22.354
In this example, the old annual recurring

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:24.507
baseline is twelve thousand dollars.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:27.155
The new commitment covers January through

00:00:27.155 --> 00:00:28.704
December twenty twenty-seven.

00:00:28.954 --> 00:00:31.530
All amounts are in dollars, before tax, with

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.178
no discounts or proration.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.268
Calling the entire purchase new sales overstates growth.

00:00:37.518 --> 00:00:39.929
Calling everything renewal hides expansion.

00:00:40.179 --> 00:00:44.326
The answer starts by classifying the components, then reconciling the

00:00:44.326 --> 00:00:48.072
customer total separately from the change in recurring value.

00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:53.149
The twelve-thousand-dollar renewal retains the existing recurring service.

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:57.172
It contributes twelve thousand dollars to the new recurring total, but

00:00:57.172 --> 00:00:58.775
zero incremental growth.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:02.865
We are carrying the baseline forward, not creating that baseline again.

00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:06.712
The additional service adds three thousand dollars per year.

00:01:06.962 --> 00:01:09.543
That is recurring expansion in this example.

00:01:09.793 --> 00:01:13.112
Compare the products and entitlements with the prior agreement

00:01:13.112 --> 00:01:16.812
so that an existing charge is not accidentally labelled as a

00:01:16.812 --> 00:01:17.601
new service.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:21.439
The fifteen-hundred-dollar commissioning fee belongs in the

00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:25.349
purchase reconciliation, but not in annual recurring revenue.

00:01:25.599 --> 00:01:29.098
Its invoice and commission treatment can follow separate rules.

00:01:29.348 --> 00:01:32.655
A payment being collected today does not make it recurring.

00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:36.877
For recurring value, start with the twelve-thousand-dollar opening

00:01:36.877 --> 00:01:37.515
baseline.

00:01:37.765 --> 00:01:40.218
There is no contraction or churn in this case.

00:01:40.468 --> 00:01:42.644
Add three thousand dollars of expansion.

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:47.338
Closing annual recurring revenue is fifteen thousand dollars, and recurring

00:01:47.338 --> 00:01:48.889
growth is three thousand.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:53.636
For the one-year purchase, add twelve thousand renewal, three thousand

00:01:53.636 --> 00:01:56.116
expansion, and fifteen hundred one-time work.

00:01:56.366 --> 00:01:59.075
That totals sixteen thousand five hundred dollars.

00:01:59.325 --> 00:02:04.419
Keep this consideration total separate from closing ARR, invoice cash, and

00:02:04.419 --> 00:02:05.576
recognized revenue.

00:02:06.233 --> 00:02:10.831
A common mistake is adding the old twelve-thousand-dollar baseline to the

00:02:10.831 --> 00:02:13.935
entire new fifteen-thousand-dollar recurring amount.

00:02:14.185 --> 00:02:16.531
That produces twenty-seven thousand dollars.

00:02:16.781 --> 00:02:20.908
The renewal already carries the retained baseline, so that calculation

00:02:20.908 --> 00:02:21.901
counts it twice.

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:26.639
If one team manages the purchase, a single commercial deal with

00:02:26.639 --> 00:02:30.119
classified components can keep the customer story together.

00:02:30.369 --> 00:02:34.966
Record retained recurring value, expansion value, and one-time value

00:02:34.966 --> 00:02:35.553
separately.

00:02:35.803 --> 00:02:39.850
Those are proposed reporting categories, not a claim that HubSpot

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.307
creates them automatically.

00:02:41.967 --> 00:02:45.986
Separate linked opportunities may help when renewal and expansion have

00:02:45.986 --> 00:02:47.663
different owners or outcomes.

00:02:47.913 --> 00:02:50.302
Keep their purchase relationship traceable.

00:02:50.552 --> 00:02:54.136
Never sum a combined parent amount and the same child amounts.

00:02:54.386 --> 00:02:58.134
A shared purchase identity does not prove that quoting across those

00:02:58.134 --> 00:02:59.933
deals works automatically.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.869
Choose your HubSpot reporting route before

00:03:02.869 --> 00:03:03.864
entering values.

00:03:04.114 --> 00:03:06.994
Deal ARR uses recurring line items.

00:03:07.244 --> 00:03:09.420
Revenue Analytics uses separately

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.895
maintained recurring revenue properties,

00:03:11.895 --> 00:03:13.473
including a monthly amount.

00:03:13.723 --> 00:03:16.342
Here, fifteen thousand dollars per year is

00:03:16.342 --> 00:03:17.841
twelve hundred fifty per month.

00:03:18.091 --> 00:03:20.235
Put the right unit in the right field,

00:03:20.235 --> 00:03:22.235
then check the date filters and account

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:22.827
access.

00:03:23.077 --> 00:03:25.974
A custom report needs its own row definition

00:03:25.974 --> 00:03:26.639
and tests.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:32.271
Define what one report row represents: for example, one purchase component.

00:03:32.521 --> 00:03:36.531
Adding associated contacts or activities can multiply rows.

00:03:36.781 --> 00:03:40.083
Add a deliberate duplicate to the test data and check that

00:03:40.083 --> 00:03:42.157
the money total stays unchanged.

00:03:42.407 --> 00:03:45.905
A distinct deal count alone does not guarantee that a money

00:03:45.905 --> 00:03:46.930
sum is correct.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.221
Now test a different outcome.

00:03:49.471 --> 00:03:52.394
The renewal succeeds, but the expansion is lost.

00:03:52.644 --> 00:03:55.631
Closing ARR should stay at twelve thousand dollars.

00:03:55.881 --> 00:03:59.653
Preserve the proposed three-thousand-dollar expansion and

00:03:59.653 --> 00:04:03.778
its lost outcome in history, rather than deleting the only evidence

00:04:03.778 --> 00:04:04.969
that it was ever offered.

00:04:05.633 --> 00:04:09.631
If the retained baseline falls to ten thousand and expansion adds

00:04:09.631 --> 00:04:13.633
three thousand, closing ARR becomes thirteen thousand.

00:04:13.883 --> 00:04:18.231
Also test future start dates: a signed expansion is not active

00:04:18.231 --> 00:04:19.515
before its effective date.

00:04:19.765 --> 00:04:24.013
Record expected and observed results separately; these examples are

00:04:24.013 --> 00:04:27.360
reporting tests, not executed HubSpot outcomes.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:31.910
Give the commission process the classified amounts, owners and policy

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:32.385
version.

00:04:32.635 --> 00:04:36.112
Do not assume every dollar earns the same rate, or that

00:04:36.112 --> 00:04:38.758
ARR growth is always the commission base.

00:04:39.008 --> 00:04:43.756
Renewal credit, expansion credit and one-time services must follow the

00:04:43.756 --> 00:04:46.048
company's actual compensation policy.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.626
Use the companion dictionary and

00:04:48.626 --> 00:04:51.009
reconciliation sheet for one purchase.

00:04:51.259 --> 00:04:53.857
Write a separate row for the retained service,

00:04:53.857 --> 00:04:56.157
expansion and one-time work, with the

00:04:56.157 --> 00:04:58.001
source reference and effective date.

00:04:58.251 --> 00:05:01.073
Record the expected total beside the actual

00:05:01.073 --> 00:05:01.984
report result.

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:05.007
If they differ, assign the discrepancy to Sales

00:05:05.007 --> 00:05:08.432
Ops and Finance, correct the classification or

00:05:08.432 --> 00:05:11.182
duplicate rows, and rerun the check before

00:05:11.182 --> 00:05:12.175
using the report.

00:05:12.833 --> 00:05:16.652
One purchase can include renewal, expansion and one-time work.

00:05:16.902 --> 00:05:20.978
In this example, the purchase is sixteen thousand five hundred dollars,

00:05:20.978 --> 00:05:25.862
closing ARR is fifteen thousand, and recurring growth is three thousand.

00:05:26.112 --> 00:05:29.803
Keep those meanings distinct, and count each contribution once.
